d 'BAYESINITS': module to generate domain-aware, chain-specific initial values for bayesmh
d
d   bayesinits generates randomized, domain-respecting initial
d values for one or more Markov chains for use with bayesmh's
d init#() options. It supports unconstrained, positive (log-scale),
d correlation (Fisher-z), Fisher-z, angular, and simplex parameter
d domains; returns chain-specific strings in r(init1)...r(initK)
d plus composite strings r(init_all) and r(init_all_wrap); and
d provides seed and rngstream controls for reproducible, dispersed
d starting values across chains. 
d
d KW: Bayesian estimation
d KW: initial values
d KW: Markov chains
d
d Requires: Stata version 15
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260915
d
d Author:  Ben Dwamena, Division of Nuclear Medicine and Molecular Imaging, University of Michigan Health System, Ann Arbor
d Support: email  bdwamena@@umich.edu
d
f bayesinits.ado
f bayesinits.sthlp
